      "writtenOn": "2025-12-09T08:34:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The only caller in third_party/pdfium/xfa/fgas/font/cfgas_fontmgr.cpp wants to see if the unicode charmap has specific chars.\n\nDoes that imply there would be a non-Unicode charmap? Does \"the Unicode charmap\" mean any particular cmap format? (If that is the case, I wonder - similar to my earlier question - why would a specific, non Unicode charmap be desirable to use?)",
      "parentUuid": "7d8d7cdb_4b208e89",
      "revId": "098475a42a947b114746a55eeebfd151d061dd60",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fe551b55_f1482282",
        "filename": "core/fxge/cfx_face.h",
